[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"482","stub":{"id":"482","section":"GA Route 5 to Dog River Reservoir","altname":"","river":"Dog","difficulty":"IIIplus","states":["USA-GEO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"23","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"110123","location":{"latitude":"33.6535987854004","longitude":"-84.8211975097656"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"115382","location":{"latitude":"33.6216011047363","longitude":"-84.7927017211914"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"7","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"877444","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877724","description":"This marks the end of the run... notice the mud stains on the rocks along the wall.  Coming down the river you will see an old house on river right.  This is looking upstream... ---edit---> After raising the level of the reservoir 10 feet, this is all deep underwater.","caption":"Facing Upstream at the Mouth - 7.3 cfs","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877444","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877444"}},{"id":"877443","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877723","description":"This picture was taken about a 1/4 mile upstream from the reservoir.  ---edit---> After raising the level of the reservoir 10 feet, this is all deep underwater.","caption":"Close to the end of the run","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"RiverSasquatch","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877443","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877443"}},{"id":"884494","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"887192","description":"The Legend Dave Collins flirting with Painted Dwayne \"The Rock\".  The easier line is to run to the left of Dwayne, but Dave plays by his own rules. ","caption":"Painted Dwayne ","poi_name":"Painted Dwayne","subject":"","author":"RiverSasquatch","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884494","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884494"}},{"id":"884496","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"887194","description":"This is the first rapid after the beach. This rapid changes its name to Little Woodall around 1000cfs.  At flows below 600, this is a very quick right to left channel with two submerged rocks in the middle of the flow. The current flushes you out of the center. There is a cheat that follows a straight channel down the extreme river right that will lead you to Painted Dwayne.","caption":"Toilet Bowl","poi_name":"Toilet Bowl","subject":"","author":"RiverSasquatch","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884496","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884496"}},{"id":"884497","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"887195","description":"Hitting the hole above The Rock.","caption":"Painted Dwayne","poi_name":"Painted Dwayne","subject":"","author":"RiverSasquatch","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884497","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884497"}},{"id":"W1OkiniCWYJiHXnUugBaz","ext":"jpg","post_id":"W1OkiniCWYJiHXnUugBaz","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"tomwaijers@yahoo.com","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-03-11T22:06:14.000Z","updated_at":"2024-03-12T02:06:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/W1OkiniCWYJiHXnUugBaz","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/W1OkiniCWYJiHXnUugBaz"}},{"id":"1649","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4158","description":"Dale playing in some random hole on the Dog River.","caption":"Dale playing on the Dog River","poi_name":"Random Hole","subject":"Dale","author":"Patrick Dortch","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1649","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1649"}},{"id":"880291","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"881408","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/880291","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/880291"}},{"id":"880292","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"881409","description":"","caption":"Dog River Rapids","poi_name":"","subject":"Mason Kirk and Kelsey Hatcher","author":"Chuck Kirk","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/880292","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/880292"}},{"id":"884495","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"887193","description":"Brad and Dave heading down YouTube rapid.  ","caption":"YouTube Rapid","poi_name":"YouTube","subject":"","author":"RiverSasquatch","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884495","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884495"}},{"id":"877445","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877725","description":"Stay left prior to entering the reservoir.  You can see a building near the boat launch straight ahead.","caption":"The Mouth - facing the reservoir @ 7.3 cfs","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877445","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877445"}}],"detail":{"id":"482","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"**Put-in** on Georgia Hwy 5, or one mile upstream at Banks Mill Rd.\n\n**Take-out** is the Dog River Reservoir at Hwy 166. The takeout is open from March thru November.\n\nThe Dog River is a good piece of whitewater if you are a Douglasville Resident.\nFor the rest of us its an exercise in beauracracy. Until 1992 the take-out was at Hwy 166. Then Douglas County built the reservoir, not seen on the topozone map. For a time you could not use the takeout/boat ramp on the reservior unless you were a douglas county resident. The current status is somewhat in limbo.\n\n**Now for more bad news:**\n\nEvidently Douglas county needs more water. So the water level on the reservior is being raised ten feet. This should occur sometime in 2006, shortly after the new bridge on Hwy 166 is completed.\n\nThe river itself is a class 3 run over bedrock ledges. At higher flows nearing floodstage it might bump up to class 4.\n\nFor more info on the rules and regulations:\n[Douglas County Water and Sewer Authority](\nhttp://www.ddcwsa.com/drinking/reservoir.html\n).","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"3.9","correlations":[{"reachID":"482","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"300","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"3000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"DOG RIVER AT GA 5, NEAR FAIRPLAY, GA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"02337410","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"23","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"3.31","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"33.6538